hadiths[18]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3746","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said, “Whoever has sex with his wife during her menstruation, he should give one dinar (maybe the narrator has doubts) and half a dinar in charity.”"
"3747","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Whoever has sex with his wife while her (menstrual) blood is (flowing), one dinar (in charity) will be required on him, and (if) yellow (material is leaking), then half a dinar (in charity) will be required."
"3748","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Whoever has sex with his wife when her discharge (of menstruation) is dark red, one dinar is required, and if it is yellow, then half a dinar is required.”"
"3749","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered one dinar in charity for a person who has intercourse with a woman during her period, and if a person has intercourse with a woman after she has become pure and before performing ghusl, then he must give half a dinar in charity."
"3750","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW): Be modest, indeed, Allah does not shy away from telling the truth."
"3751","It is narrated about Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that she had a slave and a maidservant. When Sayyida Ayesha wanted to free them, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Free the slave first."
"3752","It is narrated about Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that she had a slave and a maidservant. Sayyida Ayesha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: O Messenger of Allah, I want to free them."
"3753","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Berira: If you want to be the wife of this slave, then it is fine, and if you want to separate from him, then (it is your will) Berira separated from him."
"3754","The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: She (Barirah) was the wife of a slave, when Sayyida Aisha (RA) freed her, the Prophet (PBUH) said to her, ""If you wish, remain the wife of this slave, and if you wish, divorce her."""
"3755","The same hadith is narrated along with another document, however, it contains these words: If you agree to be the wife of this slave, take her from her. If you wish, divorce her."
"3756","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her (i.e. Sayyida Barirah) authority, her husband was a slave."
"3757","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Barira was the wife of a slave, when she (Sayyida Barira (may Allah be pleased with her) was freed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him authority over her (Barira’s) self."
"3758","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Barira's husband was a slave of Aal Abu Ahmad."
"3759","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When Berira was freed, her husband was a free man at that time."
"3760","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said to Berira, ""You go, your private parts have been freed with you."""
"3761","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Berira was the wife of a slave, she became free, so the Prophet gave her authority over her."
"3762","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Barira's husband was a slave."
"3763","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Barira's husband was a slave."
